, "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}]}, {"type": "DWS", "stimuli_ids": [], "id": 12, "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"responses": [{"selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "pdf", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob11re7pdf01.pdf"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " Talking about the new trends in management information systems! "}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Take Away"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment."}]}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}]}]}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"id": 0, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "_data": []}, {"type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"coverimg": "enpe8n4le03ob11re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "<b>Manager</b>: Today in our training session, we're going to talk about Management Information Systems. Let's start with a question. Why is this so important? </br><b>Employee 1</b>: Apart from including software systems, management information systems, or MIS, also include a set of business processes and resources necessary to gather information from functional or tactical systems. MIS is now considered a cornerstone for all management operations, and it seems that it will continue to be. </br><b>Manager</b>: That's right! But, before we meet our strategic and tactical goals, we will have to analyze and pay attention to the information collected with this system.", "image": "enpe8n4le03ob11re2img01.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"text": "<b>Employee 2</b>: What trends on management information system can we foresee? </br><b>Manager</b>: The demand for mobile digital platforms will continue to rise as a business system. More and more companies are, for example, incorporating apps into their day-to- day activities; thanks to this software application, communication between suppliers, customers and vendors is getting easier, more direct and quicker than ever. Before we notice, all of these buyer-supplier interactions will be automatized. </br><b>Employee 1</b>: Is there any other kind of interaction that we can analyze with MIS? </br><b>Manager</b>: Yes. Virtual collaboration, or VC. This type of interaction requires no physical contact between the parties involved, and it's the one we're starting to implement next week. After VC is widely assimilated by our firm, teamwork will emerge as a competitive advantage by reducing effort and time consumption in the task assigned to each of the teams.", "image": "enpe8n4le03ob11re2img02.jpg", "time": "43000", "id": 1}, {"text": "<b>Employee 2</b>: Will we have to take anything else into account? </br>\n<b>Manager</b>: Well, before reaching any strategic management decision, we'll have to conduct business intelligence. We're doing this by applying data analytics and interaction dashboard tools. As you may know, the trend for business intelligence software is growing faster than other average management information systems, and we need to keep up with it. </br>Therefore, starting next week, this company is taking a step toward this trend by applying MIS first. However, before starting this project, we'll have to check the transactional systems, the business processes and needs of management within our organization. We also need to make sure that the cost of the management information system is worth all the investment.", "image": "enpe8n4le03ob11re2img03.jpg", "time": "104500", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe8n4le03ob11re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "title": "", "id": 1, "template_override": 1, "_data": []}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "What's New in Management Information Systems"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify key information about people's jobs and places of work in spoken or written contexts.  Design the technological architecture of the IT system, through hardware and software recognition, based on available technology in the market, the analysis report and the distribution diagram."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.  Recognizes simple ideas on the design of an information system, computer architecture and hardware, and basic concepts on graphic design."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "First Conditional Using Before and After"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The First Conditional is about a real condition with a possible or imagined future consequence or result."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>The<strong> first conditional</strong> is made of two clauses. One of them is the condition and the other clause is the future consequence or result of this condition.</p> <p>Take a look at the following example:</p> <p><strong><i>Before</i></strong><i> getting meaningful and useful information, raw data will be organized, analyzed and transformed for decision-making purposes.</i></p> <p><strong>First conditional using before and after</strong>:</p> <p>It is possible to use the adverbs <strong>before</strong> and <strong>after</strong> in the conditional clause:</p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "But, before we meet our strategic and tactical goals, we will have to analyze and pay attention to the information collected with this system. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Before we notice, all of these buyer-supplier interactions will be automatized. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>Before/after\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center><b>CONDITIONAL CLAUSE (present simple tense)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center><b>RESULT/CONSEQUENCE CLAUSE (simple future - Will)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>After \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i><b>you sign</b> the contract and pay for the services,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>we <b>will provide</b> you with the software and computing infrastructure required in the cloud.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>Before \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i><b>we complete</b> this analysis, \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>all information systems <b>will be</b> taken into account. \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>The <strong>conditional clause</strong> can be started with the adverbs <strong>after </strong>and<strong> before </strong>to imply that it is very necessary to meet that condition for the consequence to happen. &nbsp;Since these two words also work as conjuctions the order of the clauses can be changed without altering the meaning:</p> <strong><i>Before</i></strong><i> the dashboard is made, we <strong>will decide</strong> how present data and what KPIs are useful.</i></br> <i>We <strong>will decide</strong> how present data and what KPIs are useful <strong>before</strong> the dashboard is made.</i></br></br> <p>Notice how the <i>comma </i>is omitted when the result clause is placed first."}, {"type": "example", "content": "After VC is widely assimilated by our firm, teamwork will emerge as a competitive advantage by reducing effort and time consumption in the task assigned to each of the teams. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "However, before starting this project, we'll have to check the transactional systems, the business processes and needs of management within our organization."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Future Simple, Present Continuous and Be Going To in Affirmative"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p><strong>The future simple</strong>, the <strong>present continuous</strong> and <strong>be going to</strong> are all tenses used to talk about the future.</p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Today in our training session, we're going to talk about Management Information Systems."}, {"type": "example", "content": "MIS is now considered a cornerstone for all management operations, and it seems that it will continue to be."}, {"type": "example", "content": "This type of interaction requires no physical contact between the parties involved, and it's the one we're starting to implement next week."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The <b>future simple</b> is used:</br><ul> <li>To state a quick decision made at the time of speaking:</br> <i><b>A</b>: The manager is here. What shall we do?</br> <b>B</b>: Don't worry, I'll talk to him.</i> </li></br>  <li>To make a prediction about the future based on non-present evidence: </br> <i>Information systems <b>will be</b> necessary in every future company. </i> </li></br>  <li>To make a promise, an offer or threat: </br> <i>We'<b>ll make</b> sure this information system is the right one for your company. </i> </li></br>  <li>To make a prediction based on a habit or predictable behavior: </br> <i>She'<b>ll need </b>to learn more about information systems if she wants to keep her job. </i> </li></ul></br>  The <b>present continuous for future</b> is used: </br><ul> <li>To  talk about future arrangements, that is, plans you have decided and organized with other people: </br> <i>Starting tomorrow, the manager <b>is verifying</b> what management information systems need improvement. </i> </li></ul>  We use <b>be going to</b>: </br><ul> <li>To talk about plans and intentions for the future: </br> <i>We'<b>re going to</b> update our management information systems. </i> </li></br>  <li>To make a prediction based on evidence we can see now: </br> <i>Look at this messy files! We'<b>re going to</b> have to change how we manage everything here soon. </i> </li></ul>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Therefore, starting next week, this company is taking a step toward this trend by applying MIS first."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "app "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a specialized program downloaded to be used online or in mobile devices"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: More and more companies are, for example, incorporating apps into their day to day activities "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob11aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "VC (virtual collaboration) "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the sharing of documents and information on which people separated geographically can work together in a synchronous or asynchronous way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: After VC is widely assimilated by our firm, teamwork will emerge as a competitive advantage by reducing effort and time consumption in the task assigned to each of the teams. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob11aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "business intelligence "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a set of technology-driven tools and techniques used to turn raw data into meaningful and useful information for decision-making purposes"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Well, before reaching any strategic management decision, we'll have to conduct business intelligence."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob11aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dashboard"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a screen that uses graphs, charts, text and numbers to summarize key information about performance in an easy-to-read way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We're doing this by applying data analytics and interaction dashboard tools."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob11aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "gather"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to collect"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Apart from including software systems, management information systems, or MIS also include a set of business processes and resources necessary to gather information from functional or tactical systems."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob11aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "transactional system "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "information processing system used in business transactions, it involves the gathering, modification and retrieval of all transaction data"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: However, before starting this project, we'll have to check the transactional systems, the business processes and needs of management within our organization.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob11aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Search for information about management information systems."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Identify trends in management information systems."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Write down a paragraph explaining possible consequences after a  company implements new trends."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your paragraph with the class and discuss about the topic."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I search for information about management information systems."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I identify trends in management information systems."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write down a paragraph explaining possible consequences after a company implements new trends."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share information and discuss about the topic. "}]}]}